1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
One train climbs so high it pipes oxygen into the cabin.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,300
I'm your China Travel Expert.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:07,100
It's the world's highest railway — Xining to Lhasa.

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:09,900
It crests Tanggula Pass at 5,072 meters.

5
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,700
Up there the air holds about half the oxygen.

6
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,300
So every seat has its own oxygen port.

7
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,600
A full day and night across the roof of the world.

8
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,900
Double-tap if you'd take this train.

9
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:23,200
★ Expert Tip: Foreigners need a Tibet Travel Permit via a licensed agency.

10
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,000
Would you fly to Lhasa — or ride up slowly?
